                <pb facs="0343" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg261"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 4.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Gorogio to Mr.
                        Portman</head>
                <p>As it has been represented that foreigners meet with inconvenience in purchasing
                    silkworm eggs from our merchants, I have again instructed the governor of
                    Kanagawa to allow this article to be as freely sold as any other article of
                    commerce.</p>
                <p>Stated for your information, in reply, with respect and esteem.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-09-07">The 16th day of the 7th month of the year of Ke-U,
                            (7th September, 1865.)</date></dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MIDLUNO IDLUMI NO KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. C. Portman,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
